.TE
.PP
The function returns as soon as no more messages are immediately
available after processing at least one, or when the timeout expires,
whichever comes first.
.PP
Internally, \f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R] uses \f[CR]select()\f[R] or
\f[CR]poll()\f[R] on the underlying file descriptor to wait for data
availability.
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]c\f[R] \(em Pointer to an authenticated \f[CR]bc_client_t\f[R]
connection.
Must not be NULL.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]timeout_ms\f[R] \(em Maximum time to wait for messages in
milliseconds.
Use 0 for non\-blocking, \-1 for indefinite wait, or a positive value
for a bounded wait.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of messages processed (>= 0) on success.
