.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R] is the central event dispatch mechanism.
All server\-push messages (observe events, debug breaks, PTY output) are
delivered through \f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
Callbacks execute synchronously in the calling thread during
\f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R].
A callback that blocks will prevent other messages from being processed.
.IP \(bu 2
It is safe to call other \f[CR]bc_*\f[R] functions (such as
\f[CR]bc_debug_continue()\f[R]) from within a callback, but not
\f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R] itself (no re\-entrant polling).
.IP \(bu 2
When using \f[CR]timeout_ms = \-1\f[R], ensure the server will
eventually send a message or that another thread can close the
connection; otherwise the call blocks indefinitely.
.IP \(bu 2
The return count includes all dispatched messages regardless of channel.
Messages with no registered callback are counted as processed
(discarded).
.IP \(bu 2
Thread safety: \f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R] must not be called concurrently with
any other operation on the same \f[CR]bc_client_t\f[R].
